---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Players Club - Contact";
---

<BaseLayout title={title}>
  <div class="content content--page" >
    <h1>Artist Statement</h1>
    <br>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2">
    <p style="text-justify: distribute;">
      I make oil paintings of things I want to put in my pocket: 
      a pigeon being cute, clouds, multicolored stripes, a waterfall, sunlight glistening through
       my water bottle. Many of these things are predictable, sometimes forgettable, 
       but holy in their own right. I paint what I think is a glimpse of heaven to keep it around me. 
       Pulling from my camera roll, I use everyday references and alter the focal point by cropping 
       and playing with positive and negative space. I transform scenes into colorful, textural homages. 
       It is curious why many of us want to hold things close to our bodies. 
       Although my work isn’t fit for a pocket, it is fit for those who look out for wondrous color 
       and patterns in this world.
    </p>
    <img src="/src/assets/IMG_8770.jpg">
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  p {
    padding: 3px;
    text-justify: auto;
    justify-content: center;
  }
</style>
